~ start

# Obligatory opener — runs once. Re-talks route through one of two entry
# greetings depending on whether the player got Splice to dance.
if GameState.get_flag("hub_post4_splice_danced", false)
	=> splice_p4_entry_dancing
if GameState.get_flag("hub_post4_splice_taunted", false)
	=> splice_p4_entry_taunted

Splice: Look at you. Standing on the right side of the wall.
Splice: Funny how that works.
=> splice_p4_questions


# Re-talk greetings. Each fires once per dialogue session because the
# questions hub self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ splice_p4_entry_taunted

Splice: Back already? The view from outside the cage that good?
=> splice_p4_questions


~ splice_p4_entry_dancing

Splice: Back already? The DJ's got taste, I'll give them that.
=> splice_p4_questions


# Single shared question hub. The dance-offer beat (with its nested
# choice) lives in its own block since Dialogue Manager doesn't support
# options nested inside an option's content.

~ splice_p4_questions

- You shouldn't have come at us.
	Splice: I came at the Gibson. You were **just** in the way.
	Splice: That'll be on the record forever, runner. Won't it.
- You okay in there?
	Splice: Not really, no.
	Splice: Quarantine's a soft jail. I get bored, I poke the walls. See what gives.
	Splice: I'm not dancing. I'm watching. Better view, honestly. Front row to every move you make.
- This is kind of cruel.
	Splice: Hmm
	Splice: It is what it is, runner. Don't lose sleep on my behalf.
	Splice: I wouldn't.
- You're not getting out. But you can dance. [#decision]
	=> dance_offer
- I won.
	Splice: Yeah. You did. Perimeters fail, runner. And I've got time.
- Was any of it real? What you believed before all this?
	Splice: All of it. That's the part you won't like.
	Splice: I built things. I gave them away.
	Splice: Then one morning I'm reading a press release. Someone I'd never met announcing my own work back to me.
	Splice: New name. Price tag.
	Splice: The people I'd given it to were lining up to pay.
	Splice: You'll see it too. Give it time.
- What's it like out there now?
	=> splice_world_subhub
- Walk away. [#exit]
	Splice: Catch you on the wire.
	do GameState.set_flag("hub_post4_splice_taunted", true)
	=> END
=> splice_p4_questions


~ dance_offer

Splice: Don't.
Splice: You don't get to forgive me, runner.
- I'm not. It's a good song.
	Splice: hmm
	Splice: It's a fine song.
	Splice: I'm not doing it for you... I'm doing it because it's a fine song.
	do GameState.set_flag("hub_post4_splice_danced", true)
	=> splice_p4_questions
- Fair enough.
	Splice: Mm.
	=> splice_p4_questions


# World sub-hub. Splice in the cage describes the world he understands.
# Calm, observational, not crowing — sentinels-style progressive
# revelation. "And everyone else?" gates on "Who's actually winning?"
# since the second beat lands harder once the first is in the room.

~ splice_world_subhub

Splice: You sure?
- Who's actually winning?
	Splice: The one percent. In wealth. In influence. In beauty.
	Splice: Here's the part that hurts — they didn't take it.
	Splice: We give it to them. Mortgages. Joining the pilgrimage of cars every morning.
	Splice: Sacrificing our time for coins to spend on the mortgage.
	do GameState.set_flag("splice_p4_asked_winning", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("splice_p4_asked_winning", false) /] And everyone else?
	Splice: They sit in bed scrolling through comments.
	Splice: Seeking a model of what's acceptable to feel in response to a thirty-second clip.
	Splice: Watching. Consuming. Eating instead of cooking.
	Splice: When they do cook, it's often with a meal kit, isn't it.
- How does it sustain itself?
	Splice: Self-interest. The cultural microwave background radiation.
	Splice: Ever-present. Taught as the bedrock of everything.
	Splice: It works, they say. How can we be anything other than self-interested?
	Splice: Who would cede an advantage in their right mind?
- Back. [#exit]
	Splice: Mm.
	=> splice_p4_questions
=> splice_world_subhub
